      "text": "The bug is in the for loop condition: `i <= items.length`. This causes an out-of-bounds access when `i` equals `items.length`, as the loop iterates over `items[i]`, which does not exist for indices beyond the array length. The correct condition should be `i < items.length`. Additionally, the initial `const total = 0;` cannot be reassigned in the loop because `const` declarations are non-reassignable, so `total +=` would throw a TypeError. The variable should be declared with `let` instead. Corrected code:\n\n```javascript\nlet total = 0;\nfor (let i = 0; i < items.length; i++) {\n  total += items[i];\n}\nreturn total;\n```",
